      "defect_type": "Type I",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "Binding material terms are required before requesting feedback, potentially forcing negotiation commitments and costs ahead of useful regulatory clarification. This is an eligibility constraint, not a mandatory transaction-approval requirement.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "Proposed \u00a7851.901(c)",
          "quote_or_absence": "the material terms of the prospective transaction must be identified in a binding written agreement or other binding document to demonstrate that the transaction is not hypothetical."
        }
      ],
      "comment_leverage": "Permit sufficiently documented nonbinding terms or an early-stage screening tier, and define which binding terms are required."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "evidence_to_intrusion_mismatch",
      "flaw_name": "Evidence-to-Intrusion Mismatch",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "The public account explains serious technology risks but does not compare risk across the entire commercial SI and biomedical scope. The prohibition\u2019s breadth warrants stronger public support; this does not deny the national-security threat.",
